    "experiments start": "Start the draft as a new Run; ends any running Run (Policy-gated). Freezes draft Targeting Rules into the Run.

Usage:
  splitch experiments start <experiment-id> [flags]

Flags:
  --app <app>              [type: string; default: SPLITCH_APP or config] App ID or slug.
  --env <environment>      [type: string; default: SPLITCH_ENV or config] Environment ID or slug.
  --body-json <json>       [type: JSON object; default: none] Request body fields; see Request body below.
  --idempotency-key <key>  [type: string; default: generated] Stable retry key for this mutation.
  --confirm                [type: boolean; default: false] Approve and apply a Policy-gated change.
  --json                   [type: boolean; default: false] Write machine-readable JSON to stdout.
  -h, --help               [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Request body (--body-json):
  review            optional  { action: "approve_and_apply" }
  reason            optional  string
  horizon           optional  string ("sequential" | "fixed")
  sampleSizeLocked  optional  number | null
  idempotency_key   required  string
  Example:
    {"horizon":"sequential","idempotency_key":"idem-1"}

Behavior:
  Start freezes the Experiment draft Targeting Rules into the new Run; the response field frozenTargetingRules is that snapshot (same as run.targetingRules).
  An empty frozen set means all Entities are eligible via allocation; Flag Configuration targeting rules do not apply while the Run is live.
  Without --json, the CLI prints a frozen-targeting summary to stderr.

Example:
  splitch experiments start <experiment-id> --body-json '{"horizon":"sequential","idempotency_key":"idem-1"}' --json",
    "experiments update": "Edit an Experiment (assignment edits gated by RUN_FROZEN / DECISION_LOCKED). Staged Targeting Rule edits under a live Run leave evaluation on the frozen Run.

Usage:
