  --json               [type: boolean; default: false] Write machine-readable JSON to stdout.
  -h, --help           [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Request body (--body-json):
  name                optional  string
  description         optional  string
  hypothesis          optional  string
  owner               optional  string
  tags                optional  string[]
  flagId              optional  string
  targetingKey        optional  string
  targetingKeyType    optional  string
  activationMetricId  optional  string | null
  allocation          optional  Record<Variant name, number>
  salt                optional  string
  variantSet          optional  { id: string; name: string; value: boolean | string | number | Record<string, unknown>; description?: string }[]
  targetingRules      optional  { id: string; flagId: string; priority: number; conditions: { attribute: string; operator: string ("eq" | "neq" | "gt" | "lt" | "gte" | "lte" | "in" | "not_in" | "matches" | "not_matches"); value: boolean | string | number | unknown[] }[]; variantId: string; percentageRollout?: { percentage: number; salt: string } | null }[]
  segmentIds          optional  string[]
  metrics             optional  { metricId: string }[]
  guardrailMetrics    optional  { metricId: string }[]
  conversionWindowMs  optional  number
  dimensions          optional  string[]
  confidenceLevel     optional  number
  stageForNextRun     optional  true
  Example:
    {"tags":[],"allocation":{"control":1,"treatment":1},"segmentIds":[],"dimensions":[],"stageForNextRun":true}

Behavior:
  While a Run is live, assignment fields (including Targeting Rules) require stageForNextRun and write only the next-Run draft.
  A successful staged Targeting Rule edit returns liveRunUnaffected naming the Run evaluation still uses.
  Without --json, the CLI prints that the live Run is unaffected.

Example:
  splitch experiments update <experiment-id> --body-json '{"tags":[],"allocation":{"control":1,"treatment":1},"segmentIds":[],"dimensions":[],"stageForNextRun":true}' --json",
    "flag-config get": "Get a Flag's per-Environment Configuration.

Usage:
  splitch flag-config get <flag-id-or-key> [flags]

Flags:
  --app <app>          [type: string; default: SPLITCH_APP or config] App ID or slug.
  --env <environment>  [type: string; default: SPLITCH_ENV or config] Environment ID or slug.
  --json               [type: boolean; default: false] Write machine-readable JSON to stdout.
  -h, --help           [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch flag-config get <flag-id-or-key> --json",
    "flag-config update": "Update enabled state / available Variants (Policy-gated change types). Turning a Flag Config off applies without approval regardless of this level.

Usage:
  splitch flag-config update <flag-id-or-key> [flags]

Flags:
  --app <app>               [type: string; default: SPLITCH_APP or config] App ID or slug.
  --env <environment>       [type: string; default: SPLITCH_ENV or config] Environment ID or slug.
  --enabled <boolean>       [type: boolean; default: current value] Set the Flag enabled state.
  --rollout <percent|none>  [type: number | none; default: current value] Set or clear the baseline rollout.
  --body-json <json>        [type: JSON object; default: none] Request body fields; see Request body below.
  --idempotency-key <key>   [type: string; default: generated] Stable retry key for this mutation.
  --confirm                 [type: boolean; default: false] Approve and apply a Policy-gated change.
  --json                    [type: boolean; default: false] Write machine-readable JSON to stdout.
  -h, --help                [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Request body (--body-json):
  enabled                optional  boolean
  availableVariantNames  optional  string[]
  rollout                optional  { percentage: number } | null
  review                 optional  { action: "approve_and_apply" }
  idempotency_key        required  string
  Example:
    {"enabled":true,"availableVariantNames":[],"idempotency_key":"idem-1"}

Example:
  splitch flag-config update <flag-id-or-key> --body-json '{"enabled":true,"availableVariantNames":[],"idempotency_key":"idem-1"}' --json",
    "flag-targeting-rules replace": "Full-replace this Environment's ordered Targeting Rule list.

Usage:
  splitch flag-targeting-rules replace <flag-id-or-key> [flags]

Flags:
  --app <app>              [type: string; default: SPLITCH_APP or config] App ID or slug.
  --env <environment>      [type: string; default: SPLITCH_ENV or config] Environment ID or slug.
  --body-json <json>       [type: JSON object; default: none] Request body fields; see Request body below.
  --idempotency-key <key>  [type: string; default: generated] Stable retry key for this mutation.
  --confirm                [type: boolean; default: false] Approve and apply a Policy-gated change.
  --json                   [type: boolean; default: false] Write machine-readable JSON to stdout.
  -h, --help               [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Request body (--body-json):
  targetingRules   required  { id: string; flagId: string; priority: number; conditions: { attribute: string; operator: string ("eq" | "neq" | "gt" | "lt" | "gte" | "lte" | "in" | "not_in" | "matches" | "not_matches"); value: boolean | string | number | unknown[] }[]; variantId: string; percentageRollout?: { percentage: number; salt: string } | null }[]
  review           optional  { action: "approve_and_apply" }
  idempotency_key  required  string
  Example:
    {"targetingRules":[{"id":"id_1","flagId":"flag_1","priority":0,"conditions":[{"attribute":"attribute","operator":"eq","value":true}],"variantId":"variant_1"}],"idempotency_key":"idem-1"}

Behavior:
  While a Run is live on this Flag, replace is refused with RUN_FROZEN (end the Run first).
  A live Run evaluates its own frozen Targeting Rule snapshot, not this Flag Configuration list.

Example:
  splitch flag-targeting-rules replace <flag-id-or-key> --body-json '{"targetingRules":[{"id":"id_1","flagId":"flag_1","priority":0,"conditions":[{"attribute":"attribute","operator":"eq","value":true}],"variantId":"variant_1"}],"idempotency_key":"idem-1"}' --json",
