    "envs": "Manage envs resources.

Usage:
  splitch envs <action> [arguments] [flags]

Commands:
  list            List an App's Environments.
  create          Create an Environment (auto-provisions its Client Key).
  get             Get one Environment (includes its inline Policy).
  update          Rename an Environment or edit its Policy.
  delete          Delete an Environment (blocked if running or last Environment).

Flags:
  -h, --help  [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch envs list --help",
    "experiment-results": "Manage experiment-results resources.

Usage:
  splitch experiment-results <action> [arguments] [flags]

Commands:
  get             Get an Experiment's results envelope: state ready with StatsOutput, state no_data naming the missing input, or state no_run naming Start when the Experiment has never had a Run.
  post            Get an Experiment's results envelope: state ready with StatsOutput, state no_data naming the missing input, or state no_run naming Start when the Experiment has never had a Run.

Flags:
  -h, --help  [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch experiment-results get --help",
    "experiments": "Manage experiments resources.

Usage:
  splitch experiments <action> [arguments] [flags]

Commands:
  list            List Experiments in an Environment.
  create          Create an Experiment draft.
  get             Get an Experiment (includes live Run id, draft config).
  update          Edit an Experiment (assignment edits gated by RUN_FROZEN / DECISION_LOCKED). Staged Targeting Rule edits under a live Run leave evaluation on the frozen Run.
  start           Start the draft as a new Run; ends any running Run (Policy-gated). Freezes draft Targeting Rules into the Run.
  delete          Archive an Experiment; Runs are retained (blocked while a Run is running).

Flags:
  -h, --help  [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch experiments list --help",
    "flag-config": "Manage flag-config resources.

Usage:
  splitch flag-config <action> [arguments] [flags]

Commands:
  get             Get a Flag's per-Environment Configuration.
  update          Update enabled state / available Variants (Policy-gated change types). Turning a Flag Config off applies without approval regardless of this level.

Flags:
  -h, --help  [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch flag-config get --help",
    "flag-targeting-rules": "Manage flag-targeting-rules resources.

Usage:
  splitch flag-targeting-rules <action> [arguments] [flags]

Commands:
  replace         Full-replace this Environment's ordered Targeting Rule list.

Flags:
  -h, --help  [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch flag-targeting-rules replace --help",
    "flag-variants": "Manage flag-variants resources.

Usage:
  splitch flag-variants <action> [arguments] [flags]

Commands:
  create          Add a Variant to the App-level catalog.
  update          Update a catalog Variant (value is Run-frozen).
  delete          Remove a catalog Variant (blocked if available or in a running Run).

Flags:
  -h, --help  [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch flag-variants create --help",
    "flags": "Manage flags resources.

Usage:
  splitch flags <action> [arguments] [flags]

Commands:
  list            List Flag definitions in an App (bounded; reports its own truncation).
  create          Create a Flag definition (key, schema, Variant catalog).
  get             Get a Flag definition by canonical id (default) or by key via ?by=key.
  update          Update a Flag definition's name/description/schema.
  delete          Delete a Flag (blocked if referenced by a running Experiment).
  promote         Promote selected Flag Configuration field-groups between Environments.
  test-eval       Dry-run resolve a Flag with the full resolution reason without firing an Exposure.
  verify          Verify a Flag KEY through the data plane without firing an Exposure.

Flags:
  -h, --help  [type: boolean; default: false] Show help and exit.

Example:
  splitch flags list --help",
